# .env first and deliberately. Everything else here is about bundle size; this
# one is about not shipping somebody's account code and port configuration
# inside a file they are about to hand to someone else. The bundle is built
# from the working tree, so a local .env would otherwise go straight in.
.env
.venv/
.git/
.github/
tests/
docs/
scripts/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
dist/
bundle/
build/
*.egg-info/
